{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:31986050","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"31986050","source":"MED","pmid":"31986050","doi":"10.1021/acs.molpharmaceut.9b01178","title":"Ketoconazole-<i>p</i>-aminobenzoic Acid Cocrystal: Revival of an Old Drug by Crystal Engineering.","authorString":"Martin F, Pop M, Kacso I, Grosu IG, Miclăuş M, Vodnar D, Lung I, Filip GA, Olteanu ED, Moldovan R, Nagy A, Filip X, Bâldea I.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Martin F","lastName":"Martin","firstName":"Flavia","initials":"F","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Molecular and Biomolecular Physics Department, National Institute for R&D of Isotopic and Molecular Technologies, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Pop M","lastName":"Pop","firstName":"Mihaela","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5555-6562"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"TeraCrystal, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Kacso I","lastName":"Kacso","firstName":"Irina","initials":"I","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1039-0543"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Molecular and Biomolecular Physics Department, National Institute for R&D of Isotopic and Molecular Technologies, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Grosu IG","lastName":"Grosu","firstName":"Ioana Georgeta","initials":"IG","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1174-2790"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Molecular and Biomolecular Physics Department, National Institute for R&D of Isotopic and Molecular Technologies, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Miclăuş M","lastName":"Miclăuş","firstName":"Maria","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9738-2417"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Molecular and Biomolecular Physics Department, National Institute for R&D of Isotopic and Molecular Technologies, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Vodnar D","lastName":"Vodnar","firstName":"Dan","initials":"D","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5407-8071"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Food Science, University of Agricultural Sciences and Veterinary Medicine Cluj-Napoca, Calea Mănăştur 3-5, 400372 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Lung I","lastName":"Lung","firstName":"Ildiko","initials":"I","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4677-4602"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Physics of Nanostructured Systems, National Institute for R&D of Isotopic and Molecular Technologies, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Filip GA","lastName":"Filip","firstName":"Gabriela Adriana","initials":"GA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Physiology, Iuliu Haţieganu University of Medicine and Pharmacy, Clinicilor 1, 400006 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Olteanu ED","lastName":"Olteanu","firstName":"Elena Diana","initials":"ED","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3034-3659"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Physiology, Iuliu Haţieganu University of Medicine and Pharmacy, Clinicilor 1, 400006 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Moldovan R","lastName":"Moldovan","firstName":"Remus","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Physiology, Iuliu Haţieganu University of Medicine and Pharmacy, Clinicilor 1, 400006 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Nagy A","lastName":"Nagy","firstName":"Andras","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9596-2899"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Toxicology, University of Agricultural Sciences and Veterinary Medicine Cluj-Napoca, Calea Mănăştur 3-5, 400372 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Filip X","lastName":"Filip","firstName":"Xenia","initials":"X","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6441-3793"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Molecular and Biomolecular Physics Department, National Institute for R&D of Isotopic and Molecular Technologies, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}},{"fullName":"Bâldea I","lastName":"Bâldea","firstName":"Ioana","initials":"I","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4046-7310"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Physiology, Iuliu Haţieganu University of Medicine and Pharmacy, Clinicilor 1, 400006 Cluj-Napoca, Romania."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5407-8071"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6441-3793"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3034-3659"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5555-6562"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7447-4925"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9596-2899"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9738-2417"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1039-0543"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1174-2790"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4046-7310"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4677-4602"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"17","journalIssueId":2917735,"dateOfPublication":"2020 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2020,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Mol Pharm","title":"Molecular pharmaceutics","essn":"1543-8392","issn":"1543-8384","nlmid":"101197791","isoabbreviation":"Mol Pharm"},"printPublicationDate":"2020-03-01"},"pubYear":"2020","pageInfo":"919-932","abstractText":"The 1:1 cocrystal of the antifungal agent ketoconazole with <i>p</i>-aminobenzoic acid was successfully crystallized and systematically characterized by a physical and pharmacological point of view. Crystal structure determination confirmed the cocrystal identity, giving full insight in its crystal packing and degree of disorder. Powder dissolution measurements revealed a 10-fold aqueous solubility increase that induces a 6.7-fold oral bioavailability improvement compared to ketoconazole. <i>In vitro</i> cell assays showed a good toxicity profile of the cocrystal with lower oxidative stress and inflammation and enhanced antifungal activity against several <i>Candida</i> species. The <i>in vivo</i> study of the cocrystal indicated similar pharmacokinetic profiles and liver toxicity with increased transaminases, as reported for ketoconazole. Notably, besides minor signs of inflammation, no morphological changes in liver parenchyma or signs of fibrosis and necrosis were detected. The enhanced solubility and oral bioavailability of the cocrystal over ketoconazole, together with the improved antifungal activity and good <i>in vitro</i>/<i>in vivo</i> toxicity, indicate its potential use as an alternative antifungal agent to the parent drug. Our results bring evidence of cocrystallization as a successful approach for bioavailability improvement of poorly soluble drugs.","affiliation":"Molecular and Biomolecular Physics Department, National Institute for R&D of Isotopic and Molecular Technologies, 67-103 Donat, 400293 Cluj-Napoca, Romania.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Autoritatea Nationala pentru Cercetare Stiintifica","grantId":"PN-III-P2-2.1-PED-2016-1521  (157PED)","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Fibroblasts","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierNa